            <tr><th scope="row">Setup fees</th><td>Usually low</td><td>Usually low</td><td>Commonly charged by design and color</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Turnaround</th><td class="compare-best">Same-day may be available</td><td class="compare-best">Same-day may be available</td><td>Usually requires more setup time</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Colors and photo detail</th><td>Full color, gradients, and fine photo detail</td><td>Full color, bright whites, gradients, and fine detail</td><td>Excellent spot colors; photo work needs more complex separations and setup</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Estimated cost at 1 piece*</th><td class="compare-best">About $25</td><td class="compare-best">About $25</td><td>Usually not economical for one shirt</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Estimated cost at 12 pieces*</th><td class="compare-best">About $18 each</td><td class="compare-best">About $18 each</td><td>Setup can keep the per-shirt price higher, especially with multiple colors</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Estimated cost at 100 pieces*</th><td>About $15 each</td><td>About $15 each</td><td class="compare-best">Can be the lowest-cost choice for a simple one- or two-color design</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Feel on fabric</th><td>Soft and breathable, especially on light cotton garments</td><td>Smooth, slightly raised transfer feel; large solid areas feel less breathable</td><td>Varies by ink and coverage, from soft water-based prints to a heavier ink layer</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Durability</th><td>Good when properly cured and cared for</td><td>Very good when properly applied and cared for</td><td>Excellent when properly printed and cured</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Best fabric matches</th><td>Cotton and cotton-rich blends</td><td>Cotton, polyester, blends, and many heat-compatible items</td><td>Many fabrics when the correct ink system is used</td></tr>
