        <span class="compare-kicker">The honest answer</span>
        <h2>When screen printing makes more sense</h2>
        <p class="compare-intro">Screen printing can be the better production method for a very large run using one or two solid ink colors. Once the screens are prepared, repeating the same simple design across hundreds of identical garments can bring the unit price down.</p>
        <p class="compare-intro">It can also be a strong fit when a project requires a particular specialty ink or a traditional printed finish. Image On does not provide that process, but we would rather explain the tradeoff clearly than recommend the wrong method for your order.</p>
        <p><a href="/services/custom-t-shirts/">Explore Image On's custom T-shirt printing services →</a></p>
      </div>
