      <span class="compare-kicker">Frequently asked questions</span>
      <h2>DTG, DTF, and same-day shirt questions</h2>
      <div class="compare-faqs">
        <details open><summary>Is DTG as good as screen printing?</summary><p>Yes, for the right project. DTG is an excellent choice for cotton shirts, small or medium quantities, photo-quality artwork, gradients, and a soft feel. Screen printing may be more economical for very large runs with one or two simple colors.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does DTF crack or peel?</summary><p>A properly applied DTF transfer is designed to be durable, but incorrect application, excessive heat, harsh chemicals, and repeated high-temperature drying can shorten its life. Wash inside out in cool water and follow the shop's care instructions.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I get custom shirts same day in San Diego?</summary><p>Same-day DTG or DTF service may be available through Image On's Santee, Downtown San Diego, and Oceanside shops. Availability depends on artwork, garment stock, quantity, placement, and the current production schedule, so call the preferred location first.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What's the minimum order?</summary><p>Image On does not require a minimum for DTG or DTF custom shirts. You can ask about one shirt, a dozen, or a larger group order. Pricing per shirt generally improves as quantity increases.</p></details>
